; Trino ODBC driver -- odbcinst.ini template.
;
; Placeholders (replaced by packaging/linux/register_driver.sh, packaging/macos/postinstall.sh or by
; hand):
;   @TRINO_ODBC_DRIVER_NAME@   registered driver name (default: "Trino ODBC Driver")
;   @TRINO_ODBC_DRIVER_PATH@   absolute path of libtrinoodbc.so / libtrinoodbc.dylib
;   @TRINO_ODBC_VERSION@       driver version (default: 1.0.0)
;
; Usage with unixODBC:   odbcinst -i -d -f <this file, placeholders substituted, WITHOUT the
;                        [ODBC Drivers] section and the comment lines> -- odbcinst installs every
;                        section of the file as a driver, so leaving [ODBC Drivers] in would register
;                        a phantom driver called "ODBC Drivers" (the packaging scripts strip it)
; Usage with iODBC:      merge the [ODBC Drivers] entry and append the driver section to
;                        /Library/ODBC/odbcinst.ini (macOS) or ~/.odbcinst.ini
;
; There is deliberately no Setup= key: on Unix the library exports no ConfigDSN /
; ODBCINSTGetProperties, so a GUI administrator that loaded it as a setup library would fail.
;
; The same section format is understood by unixODBC, iODBC and the Starburst/Simba driver's
; odbcinst.ini, so a DSN written for that driver only needs the Driver= line changed.

[ODBC Drivers]
@TRINO_ODBC_DRIVER_NAME@=Installed

[@TRINO_ODBC_DRIVER_NAME@]
Description=Trino ODBC Driver @TRINO_ODBC_VERSION@ (ODBC 3.8, Unicode)
Driver=@TRINO_ODBC_DRIVER_PATH@
APILevel=2
ConnectFunctions=YYN
DriverODBCVer=03.80
FileUsage=0
SQLLevel=1
UsageCount=1
